@title Message Queue for Order Routing
@subtitle Decision page for the architecture review on 2026-10-21, Fulfillment team at Saltmarsh Foods

Expected load is 1800 messages per second at peak and 400 on average, with messages under 8 KB. At-least-once delivery is acceptable, and ordering is needed only per order.

## Options

- **SQS**: managed queue service with FIFO queues.
- **Kafka (Amazon MSK)**: managed Apache Kafka cluster.
- **RabbitMQ (Amazon MQ)**: managed RabbitMQ broker.

## Comparison

table = Option,Ordering,Throughput ceiling,Ops burden,Replay,Monthly cost; SQS,FIFO per message group,very high,none,no,$310; Kafka (Amazon MSK),per partition,very high,high,yes up to retention,"$1,450"; RabbitMQ (Amazon MQ),per queue,medium,medium,no,$690

data cost = option,usd; SQS,310; Kafka,1450; RabbitMQ,690

chart bar cost y=usd unit=$ labels title="Estimated monthly cost"

## Pros and cons

### SQS

**Pros**

- Fully managed and scales automatically.

**Cons**

- No replay.
- 256 KB message limit.

### Kafka (Amazon MSK)

**Pros**

- Replay and stream processing.

**Cons**

- Needs partition planning.
- Needs broker upgrades.

### RabbitMQ (Amazon MQ)

**Pros**

- Flexible routing.
- Mature client support across languages.

**Cons**

- We would own capacity planning.
- Medium throughput ceiling.

## Recommendation

! Recommend SQS with FIFO queues keyed by order ID. It meets our load, ordering and at-least-once needs at the lowest monthly cost of the three.

We will revisit this if the analytics team needs event replay in 2027.
